From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:49:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Name the engine Purr

Godot's trademark policy doesn't allow a fork to present itself as
Godot Engine, so the editor title, version string, startup header and
crash logs now say Purr, and the startup header links Purr's website.
The editor's crash message points to Purr rather than Godot's issue
tracker, since Purr's bugs are Purr's to fix. The version number stays
Godot's, so the version still shows which release Purr is based on.

The short name also changes, which gives Purr its own data folder
(Application Support/Purr, %APPDATA%\Purr, ~/.local/share/purr).
Without it, Purr and stock Godot of the same version would share one
export_templates folder and overwrite each other's templates. Games'
user:// folders move to the Purr folder too.

The build's module search knows the renamed tree as an engine too, so
a custom_modules path that holds one isn't searched as modules.

Test: start the editor; its title, the startup header and --version say
Purr, and it keeps its settings in Application Support/Purr (or the
platform's equivalent).

Not for upstream. Policy: https://godotengine.org/trademark/
---
 godot/core/config/project_settings.cpp | 2 +-
 godot/methods.py                       | 6 ++++--
 godot/version.py                       | 6 +++---
 3 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/godot/core/config/project_settings.cpp b/godot/core/config/project_settings.cpp
index 4cf864f9..9d8267cd 100644
--- a/godot/core/config/project_settings.cpp
+++ b/godot/core/config/project_settings.cpp
@@ -1820,7 +1820,7 @@ ProjectSettings::ProjectSettings() {
 	GLOBAL_DEF("debug/settings/crash_handler/message",
 			String("Please include this when reporting the bug to the project developer."));
 	GLOBAL_DEF("debug/settings/crash_handler/message.editor",
-			String("Please include this when reporting the bug on: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues"));
+			String("Please include this when reporting the bug on: https://oss.nekolab.studio/purr"));
 	GLOBAL_DEF_RST(PropertyInfo(Variant::INT, "rendering/occlusion_culling/bvh_build_quality", PROPERTY_HINT_ENUM, "Low,Medium,High"), 2);
 	GLOBAL_DEF_RST("rendering/occlusion_culling/jitter_projection", true);
 
diff --git a/godot/methods.py b/godot/methods.py
index 3dca5ad6..af8e87ad 100644
--- a/godot/methods.py
+++ b/godot/methods.py
@@ -264,8 +264,10 @@ def detect_modules(search_path, recursive=False):
         version_path = os.path.join(path, "version.py")
         if os.path.exists(version_path):
             with open(version_path, "r", encoding="utf-8") as f:
-                if 'short_name = "godot"' in f.read():
-                    return True
+                version = f.read()
+            # Purr's own tree as well as Godot's.
+            if 'short_name = "godot"' in version or 'short_name = "purr"' in version:
+                return True
         return False
 
     def get_files(path):
diff --git a/godot/version.py b/godot/version.py
index 6569e62c..b9f237b9 100644
--- a/godot/version.py
+++ b/godot/version.py
@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@
-short_name = "godot"
-name = "Godot Engine"
+short_name = "purr"
+name = "Purr"
 major = 4
 minor = 8
 patch = 0
 status = "beta"
 module_config = ""
-website = "https://godotengine.org"
+website = "https://oss.nekolab.studio/purr"
 docs = "latest"
